{"title":"Career Roadmap · Jewellery Designer","role":"Jewellery Designer","summary":"A Jewellery Designer develops concepts and designs for jewellery and accessories by combining aesthetics, craftsmanship, materials, gemstones, ergonomics, manufacturing, CAD, trend research, and brand identity. The role can range from handcrafted jewellery and bespoke pieces to digitally modelled, mass-produced and luxury collections.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Des (Bachelor of Design)","Course":"Jewellery / Accessory Design"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Approx. Timeline","Target"],"rows":[[{"text":"Foundation"},{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Design fundamentals + jewellery materials"}],[{"text":"Craft Skills"},{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Jewellery making + techniques"}],[{"text":"Digital Design"},{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"CAD + gemstone + production knowledge"}],[{"text":"Industry Preparation"},{"text":"Year 4"},{"text":"Internship + collection portfolio"}],[{"text":"Entry"},{"text":"0–2 years"},{"text":"Junior Jewellery Designer"}],[{"text":"Growth"},{"text":"3–6 years"},{"text":"Jewellery Designer / Senior Designer"}],[{"text":"Mid Career"},{"text":"6–10 years"},{"text":"Design Lead"}],[{"text":"Leadership"},{"text":"10–15 years"},{"text":"Design Head / Creative Director"}],[{"text":"Long-term"},{"text":"15+ years"},{"text":"Jewellery Brand / Independent Designer"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build Each Year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Design & Jewellery Foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Build fundamentals in:"},{"type":"h","text":"Design"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Drawing"},{"text":"Sketching"},{"text":"Form"},{"text":"Proportion"},{"text":"Composition"},{"text":"Colour"},{"text":"Texture"},{"text":"Visual balance"},{"text":"Design thinking"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Jewellery fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","